# width: 120
# `ui.dock.mode = .always` (src/app/launcher_dock.zig): the launcher
# dock — macOS's Dock, not the bottom panel and not the dock widgets —
# reserves the OUTERMOST row of the editor area and lists the enabled
# integrations, then the terminals, then whatever `ui.dock.pins` names.
#
# At 120x40 that row is 39 — the SCREEN's last row, under the `:` line
# (which moves to 38 and the statusline to 37), because the dock is the
# frame's outermost edge in every mode and that is the row its reveal
# band watches when it is down. The click below is the proof: if the
# strip were anywhere else it would land on the `:` row instead.
write a.txt "alpha\n"
open a.txt
expect screen lacks "New terminal"
ex dock always
expect screen contains "dock: always"
# Browser is the one integration chip enabled out of the box; the
# terminals follow it.
expect screen contains "Browser"
expect screen contains "New terminal"
# The pin chip lives at the strip's end.
expect screen contains "󰐃"
# A click on New terminal opens a shell…
click 16 39
wait 900
expect pane Terminal
# …and the shell joins the strip as a running item, wearing the dot
# macOS puts under an open app.
expect screen contains "●"
